  "discussion": {
    "headline": "Brisk, chilly and unpleasant weekend",
    "dateLine": "Brief 12:30 p.m. Friday, November 13, 2026, Update",
    "excerpt": "As expected, rainfall amounts increased dramatically from southwest-to-northeast across the Lower Susquehanna Valley since Thursday morning. Less than 0.10\" of rain fell in most of Franklin County, while eastern Lancaster County and areas near Philadelphia received a general 0.75-1.25\" (see below). Some strong-to-severe thunderstorms even erupted early Thursday afternoon and produced large hail in parts of southeastern PA. …",
